1
00:00:03,611 --> 00:00:05,775
(street noise)

2
00:00:10,253 --> 00:00:12,932
So, we're in the biggest
shopping district in Tokyo.

3
00:00:13,420 --> 00:00:16,220
And a crowd of people
has amassed, to, uh...

4
00:00:16,632 --> 00:00:19,143
to stroke
several cats in a pram.

5
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:20,408
(laughs)

6
00:00:20,908 --> 00:00:23,206
And I say that
without much surprise

7
00:00:23,231 --> 00:00:25,228
because I'm kind of
used to

8
00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:27,118
seeing this kind of stuff
in Japan.

9
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:29,347
If you're walking past,

10
00:00:29,372 --> 00:00:31,685
it just looks like a
pile of rugs in a pram.

11
00:00:32,340 --> 00:00:33,940
And as you get closer,
you see the paws

12
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:35,102
like hanging out the edge,

13
00:00:35,631 --> 00:00:38,161
and as you get even more closer,
you see ten cats sleeping.

14
00:00:39,517 --> 00:00:41,757
Look at all these paws
hanging off the edge here.

15
00:00:44,342 --> 00:00:45,361
(meowing)

16
00:00:45,432 --> 00:00:47,872
(playful instrumental music)

17
00:00:48,832 --> 00:00:49,984
Japan has long been

18
00:00:50,009 --> 00:00:52,532
a source of confusion
for foreign travellers

19
00:00:52,557 --> 00:00:54,507
and as a British guy
who's has lived here

20
00:00:54,540 --> 00:00:55,948
for almost five years now,

21
00:00:55,973 --> 00:00:58,563
in many ways I'm still as
surprised and bewildered by it

22
00:00:58,588 --> 00:01:00,194
as the day that I arrived.

23
00:01:01,563 --> 00:01:02,788
My name's Chris Broad

24
00:01:02,788 --> 00:01:05,312
and I spend my time
as a YouTube vlogger in Japan

25
00:01:05,340 --> 00:01:07,064
going in search
of the beautiful,

26
00:01:07,089 --> 00:01:09,035
the unique and the bizarre.

27
00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:11,893
From sake vending machines
and capsule hotels

28
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:14,979
to a man casually walking
through central Tokyo

29
00:01:15,020 --> 00:01:17,277
with a stroller
stuffed full of cats.

30
00:01:18,540 --> 00:01:20,404
It's a theme that you encounter

31
00:01:20,429 --> 00:01:22,154
pretty much everyday in Japan.

32
00:01:22,578 --> 00:01:23,678
Cats.

33
00:01:24,426 --> 00:01:26,802
The Japanese have an
absolute obsession with them

34
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:29,039
and not just as pets, either.

35
00:01:30,465 --> 00:01:32,809
I'm setting off on a journey
across the country

36
00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:35,436
to uncover
this cat obsessed culture,

37
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:37,100
where we'll explore everything

38
00:01:37,124 --> 00:01:39,227
from questionable
office practices

39
00:01:39,260 --> 00:01:41,218
and iconic cat characters

40
00:01:41,757 --> 00:01:44,523
to famous cats that work
as mascots in shops,

41
00:01:44,727 --> 00:01:46,206
and even train stations.

42
00:01:47,020 --> 00:01:49,268
We're off to discover what
makes Japan

43
00:01:49,363 --> 00:01:51,035
a cat nation

44
00:01:51,103 --> 00:01:53,530
(playful instrumental music)
(meowing)

45
00:01:59,260 --> 00:02:02,220
(water running)

46
00:02:02,688 --> 00:02:06,438
(playful instrumental music)

47
00:02:08,483 --> 00:02:12,062
Our first stop is one of
Tokyo's largest cat cafes.

48
00:02:12,159 --> 00:02:14,151
The best way
to describe a cat cafe

49
00:02:14,180 --> 00:02:16,939
is a coffee shop where
customers can relax and unwind

50
00:02:17,294 --> 00:02:19,167
in the presence
of dozens of cats.

51
00:02:20,722 --> 00:02:22,652
Whilst cat cafes
have started springing up

52
00:02:22,677 --> 00:02:24,392
all over the world as gimmicks,

53
00:02:24,683 --> 00:02:27,067
in Japanese cities they're
a common appearance.

54
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:28,380
And far from being a gimmick,

55
00:02:28,424 --> 00:02:30,528
the resolution
to a common problem.

56
00:02:31,136 --> 00:02:33,480
As a huge proportion
of Japan's population

57
00:02:33,545 --> 00:02:36,248
live in apartments where
pets are forbidden,

58
00:02:36,506 --> 00:02:39,709
the cat cafe allows customers
to effortlessly indulge

59
00:02:39,899 --> 00:02:41,741
in their passion for cats.

60
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:45,590
(playful instrumental music)

61
00:02:51,531 --> 00:02:53,323
So, this is the food
and drink menu.

62
00:02:53,348 --> 00:02:56,531
You can sit here,
eat your spaghetti bolognese,

63
00:02:56,794 --> 00:02:59,463
drink your ginger ale
and stroke the cats.

64
00:02:59,942 --> 00:03:00,953
It's pretty popular,

65
00:03:00,978 --> 00:03:02,632
that's what a lot of
locals come here to do.

66
00:03:02,871 --> 00:03:04,229
I can't believe it, personally,

67
00:03:04,371 --> 00:03:06,839
something seems a bit wrong
about eating

68
00:03:07,131 --> 00:03:10,421
a seafood platter surrounded
by 50 cats in a room

69
00:03:10,460 --> 00:03:13,722
where there's fur just
everywhere in the air.

70
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:16,020
The highlight is undoubtedly

71
00:03:16,077 --> 00:03:18,001
the sheer variety
of cats to be found.

72
00:03:18,458 --> 00:03:20,530
From fluffy cats
and grumpy cats

73
00:03:20,890 --> 00:03:22,564
to cats with stumpy legs.

74
00:03:22,753 --> 00:03:25,193
It's like cat tapas.

75
00:03:26,087 --> 00:03:28,463
This is the shy one that
I saw a poster about.

76
00:03:29,379 --> 00:03:31,388
And he's very long,

77
00:03:32,058 --> 00:03:33,433
he's like a sausage cat.

78
00:03:35,587 --> 00:03:36,691
What's he looking at?

79
00:03:36,836 --> 00:03:38,404
There's genuinely nothing
round there,

80
00:03:38,463 --> 00:03:41,093
he's just having fun looking
around the corner of the door.

81
00:03:41,579 --> 00:03:45,329
(playful instrumental music)

82
00:03:47,618 --> 00:03:50,155
This one has just been sat
here for the last 20 minutes

83
00:03:50,329 --> 00:03:53,391
just drinking this water
from this pink bowl.

84
00:03:56,858 --> 00:03:59,390
To the untrained eye
it's merely a light.

85
00:03:59,529 --> 00:04:00,809
If you come around here,

86
00:04:01,402 --> 00:04:04,064
there's actually a cat
sleeping up there on the light.

87
00:04:06,003 --> 00:04:07,012
Oh my God.

88
00:04:07,185 --> 00:04:08,218
How did he get up there?

89
00:04:09,195 --> 00:04:10,576
There's no easy way to get up.

90
00:04:14,021 --> 00:04:15,035
Oh...

91
00:04:15,297 --> 00:04:17,038
I think this might be
one of the cats to avoid.

92
00:04:18,384 --> 00:04:20,357
On the sign
at the front it said

93
00:04:20,380 --> 00:04:22,156
"Don't touch these four cats."

94
00:04:22,801 --> 00:04:24,925
Because they don't like people,

95
00:04:25,055 --> 00:04:27,314
and they will eat your face.

96
00:04:30,176 --> 00:04:31,830
I'm a bit scared of this one.

97
00:04:31,935 --> 00:04:33,368
And the fact
that he's got a sweater on,

98
00:04:34,074 --> 00:04:35,187
like a gangster cat.

99
00:04:35,809 --> 00:04:37,145
Not all cats are in the mood

100
00:04:37,170 --> 00:04:38,760
to be fondled
by strangers though,

101
00:04:38,906 --> 00:04:40,040
and on the wall of the cafe,

102
00:04:40,151 --> 00:04:42,251
you'll find a profile
of each of the cats,

103
00:04:42,276 --> 00:04:44,969
complete with their name
and personality traits.

104
00:04:45,118 --> 00:04:48,087
Sometimes including a
warning on who to avoid.

105
00:04:48,412 --> 00:04:50,113
After all, no one
wants to walk out

106
00:04:50,138 --> 00:04:52,441
of a cat cafe
without their face.

107
00:04:53,420 --> 00:04:55,013
Well, there's
a little warning here.

108
00:04:55,456 --> 00:04:56,844
This cat called Umichan,

109
00:04:57,519 --> 00:04:58,841
"She is so shy cat.

110
00:04:59,259 --> 00:05:00,867
Sometimes
she'll bite your finger.

111
00:05:01,222 --> 00:05:02,449
Please be careful."

112
00:05:03,479 --> 00:05:07,014
The thing is, Umichan, looks
like about four different cats

113
00:05:07,039 --> 00:05:08,286
that I've seen
in this room already,

114
00:05:08,833 --> 00:05:10,647
so I don't know
which one to avoid.

115
00:05:11,780 --> 00:05:13,260
I probably will get bitten.

116
00:05:13,671 --> 00:05:15,709
I've seen quite a few
different notices

117
00:05:15,886 --> 00:05:17,795
around the place saying
"Avoid this cat."

118
00:05:18,295 --> 00:05:19,582
"Don't feed this cat any food
because

119
00:05:19,582 --> 00:05:20,869
it's got kidney disease."

120
00:05:20,912 --> 00:05:22,241
There's lots
of different descriptions

121
00:05:22,327 --> 00:05:23,705
and disclaimers
around the place.

122
00:05:26,582 --> 00:05:28,669
This is a book of all the cats.

123
00:05:29,423 --> 00:05:31,013
You see pictures of them,
their name,

124
00:05:31,762 --> 00:05:34,466
where they're from,
their birthday.

125
00:05:35,602 --> 00:05:37,179
I think this
is the gangster cat,

126
00:05:38,104 --> 00:05:39,362
and his name is Nats.

127
00:05:39,925 --> 00:05:41,802
Ironic because
he's a little bit nuts.

128
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:45,366
Whoa!

129
00:05:45,801 --> 00:05:46,816
Did you see that?

130
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:48,900
This cat's mental.

131
00:05:52,787 --> 00:05:54,770
Cat cafe is maybe ideal
for someone

132
00:05:54,780 --> 00:05:57,054
with a busy lifestyle
and a cramped apartment.

133
00:05:57,459 --> 00:05:59,363
But what if you really want
to experience cats

134
00:05:59,380 --> 00:06:01,402
in their element
out in the wild,

135
00:06:01,867 --> 00:06:04,261
a place where all the cats
can roam free?

136
00:06:04,612 --> 00:06:07,196
Meow, meow, meow, meow.
(meowing)

137
00:06:11,584 --> 00:06:13,262
Hidden away
off the northeast coast

138
00:06:13,262 --> 00:06:17,378
is a mysterious island home
to hundreds of feral cats.

139
00:06:17,378 --> 00:06:18,913
And my good friend,
Natsuki, and I

140
00:06:18,913 --> 00:06:20,438
have hopped on a boat
to go and explore

141
00:06:20,438 --> 00:06:22,518
the infamous island
of Tashirojima,

142
00:06:22,518 --> 00:06:24,435
and discover its story.

143
00:06:26,004 --> 00:06:29,623
There's a bit of a Jurassic
Park vibe given the fog.

144
00:06:29,623 --> 00:06:32,271
The whole boat
is enshrouded by fog.

145
00:06:32,271 --> 00:06:34,708
Everybody is so happy and
excited to see the dinosaurs,

146
00:06:34,708 --> 00:06:36,862
except the dinosaurs are cats.

147
00:06:38,843 --> 00:06:40,838
Today there are numerous
islands around Japan

148
00:06:40,838 --> 00:06:43,926
that like to refer to
themselves as a cat island.

149
00:06:43,926 --> 00:06:45,429
As many islands have worked out,

150
00:06:45,429 --> 00:06:48,621
it's a brilliant way to bring
in bucket loads of tourists

151
00:06:48,621 --> 00:06:51,873
to places that are typically
completely isolated.

152
00:06:52,825 --> 00:06:55,972
But Tashirojima is considered
to be the original cat island

153
00:06:55,972 --> 00:06:59,527
that initially started this
trend about a decade ago.

154
00:06:59,955 --> 00:07:01,429
And true to its reputation,

155
00:07:01,429 --> 00:07:03,432
no sooner
have we hopped off the boat,

156
00:07:03,432 --> 00:07:05,069
we find ourselves surrounded

157
00:07:05,069 --> 00:07:07,407
by the island's
fluffy inhabitants.

158
00:07:07,470 --> 00:07:09,797
(playful instrumental music)

159
00:07:11,629 --> 00:07:14,881
This is quite
a strange, surreal place.

160
00:07:15,511 --> 00:07:18,954
Just a port with dozens of cats.

161
00:07:21,270 --> 00:07:22,752
Just relaxing under the boat.

162
00:07:24,770 --> 00:07:27,051
(bird caws in background)

163
00:07:35,517 --> 00:07:36,964
There's five cats
on the roof here,

164
00:07:37,595 --> 00:07:39,315
and there's some kind
of fight going on,

165
00:07:39,866 --> 00:07:40,969
it's kind of tense.

166
00:07:42,413 --> 00:07:44,203
I've never seen
so many cats on a roof.

167
00:07:46,135 --> 00:07:48,391
It's funny to think
this is someone's house.

168
00:07:50,133 --> 00:07:55,182
And there's like 20 people
around the house (laughs).

169
00:07:56,498 --> 00:07:58,003
Just like the cats
which inhabit them,

170
00:07:58,083 --> 00:08:01,612
each island is unique, with
its own history and folktales.

171
00:08:01,688 --> 00:08:03,929
Here, at Tashirojima,
the most popular legend

172
00:08:03,929 --> 00:08:06,434
says that fishermen
brought cats to the island

173
00:08:06,459 --> 00:08:09,178
because they believed they
could predict fishing trends.

174
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:13,150
Others say that cats were
brought here by silk merchants,

175
00:08:13,175 --> 00:08:15,493
eager to protect their
silk worms from mice.

176
00:08:15,816 --> 00:08:17,092
Whatever the original intent,

177
00:08:17,092 --> 00:08:20,412
the island is now completely
overrun with hundreds of cats,

178
00:08:20,437 --> 00:08:24,078
outnumbering the island's
human population six to one.

179
00:08:24,685 --> 00:08:27,384
In Japanese culture,
cats are considered a symbol

180
00:08:27,482 --> 00:08:28,974
of good fortune and wealth,

181
00:08:28,974 --> 00:08:31,715
and the cats on this island
have certainly promoted it,

182
00:08:31,715 --> 00:08:34,240
resulting in the port
recently being upgraded

183
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:36,659
to handle the increasing
number of tourists

184
00:08:36,684 --> 00:08:38,807
who flock to the island
every month.

185
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:41,620
It is remarkable to think
that the cats have brought

186
00:08:41,624 --> 00:08:45,243
so much economic prosperity
to this remote island.

187
00:08:46,460 --> 00:08:51,020
It's very elegant, a very
elegant, confident cat.

188
00:08:51,404 --> 00:08:52,571
And beautiful.

189
00:08:55,811 --> 00:08:57,893
- It does look like a
blanket with legs on it.

190
00:08:57,893 --> 00:09:01,171
- A nice blanket, yeah.
(laughing)

191
00:09:06,540 --> 00:09:08,020
In recent times, Tashirojima

192
00:09:08,025 --> 00:09:10,193
was very close to the epicenter

193
00:09:10,193 --> 00:09:12,553
of the great Tōhoku earthquake
and tsunami

194
00:09:12,553 --> 00:09:16,134
that destroyed much of the
northeast coastline in 2011.

195
00:09:16,460 --> 00:09:18,340
And although the island
suffered much damage,

196
00:09:18,347 --> 00:09:20,607
some locals credit
the cat's fortune

197
00:09:20,607 --> 00:09:22,777
for protecting the island
from what could've been

198
00:09:22,777 --> 00:09:24,616
far greater devastation.

199
00:09:25,684 --> 00:09:27,637
Metal poles
across the island indicate

200
00:09:27,637 --> 00:09:30,509
the terrifying height on
which the waves struck

201
00:09:30,509 --> 00:09:31,960
on that tragic day.

202
00:09:37,276 --> 00:09:40,776
(slow instrumental music)

203
00:09:41,666 --> 00:09:43,506
The idea of cats
bringing good fortune

204
00:09:43,531 --> 00:09:46,045
has long been
a part of Japanese folklore.

205
00:09:46,380 --> 00:09:48,580
The iconic beckoning cat statue

206
00:09:48,589 --> 00:09:50,604
can be seen
all across the country.

207
00:09:50,828 --> 00:09:52,426
Known as the maneki-neko,

208
00:09:52,585 --> 00:09:55,123
they're said to bring good luck
and fortune to merchants,

209
00:09:55,233 --> 00:09:57,659
families and even those
suffering from illness.

210
00:09:58,340 --> 00:10:00,940
And today, they can be seen
in practically

211
00:10:00,965 --> 00:10:03,528
every store, restaurant
and place of business.

212
00:10:04,220 --> 00:10:05,740
But how did it all start?

213
00:10:06,020 --> 00:10:08,500
The origins of the maneki-neko
statue aren't clear,

214
00:10:08,508 --> 00:10:11,347
but one popular legend holds
that they can be traced back

215
00:10:11,660 --> 00:10:13,732
several hundred years
to this temple.

216
00:10:14,453 --> 00:10:15,634
According to the tale,

217
00:10:15,634 --> 00:10:18,045
a feudal lord was passing
by the temple one day

218
00:10:18,060 --> 00:10:21,242
when he saw a lone cat
beckoning him inside.

219
00:10:21,267 --> 00:10:22,423
The lord entered the temple,

220
00:10:22,423 --> 00:10:25,595
and in doing so avoided
a violent thunderstorm

221
00:10:25,620 --> 00:10:26,721
that suddenly erupted.

222
00:10:26,860 --> 00:10:29,203
Thankful, the lord
decided to honor the cat.

223
00:10:29,340 --> 00:10:30,403
When it passed away,

224
00:10:30,443 --> 00:10:33,294
he had a shrine built for
it here at the temple.

225
00:10:34,605 --> 00:10:35,722
How many are there?

226
00:10:37,127 --> 00:10:39,590
There must be like 10,000,
I don't know.

227
00:10:40,403 --> 00:10:41,439
There's so many

228
00:10:42,140 --> 00:10:43,185
of different sizes,

229
00:10:43,420 --> 00:10:44,787
and they're all
doing the same pose.

230
00:10:45,130 --> 00:10:46,480
It's actually kind of creepy.

231
00:10:47,660 --> 00:10:48,700
But awesome.

232
00:10:49,500 --> 00:10:51,940
Another folktale about the
origins of the beckoning cat

233
00:10:51,946 --> 00:10:53,927
says that
an impoverished store owner

234
00:10:53,927 --> 00:10:56,578
took in a stray cat one
day and out of gratitude,

235
00:10:56,578 --> 00:10:59,127
the cat started waving in
new customers,

236
00:10:59,275 --> 00:11:01,679
bringing great prosperity
to the business.

237
00:11:02,674 --> 00:11:04,418
Whether you choose to
believe the beckoning cat

238
00:11:04,443 --> 00:11:07,423
was an ancient weatherman
or a brilliant salesman,

239
00:11:07,423 --> 00:11:09,507
the maneki-neko stands
as Japan's

240
00:11:09,507 --> 00:11:12,302
undisputed symbol of
good luck and fortune.

241
00:11:14,150 --> 00:11:15,560
Spot the odd cat out?

242
00:11:17,338 --> 00:11:18,400
About a billion cats,

243
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:19,751
and one with a mustache.

244
00:11:21,083 --> 00:11:22,330
I wonder how this started.

245
00:11:22,330 --> 00:11:23,934
Did someone just put one down,

246
00:11:23,934 --> 00:11:27,674
and then another person
thought, "Yeah, another one,"

247
00:11:28,223 --> 00:11:30,206
and it just got out of control?

248
00:11:31,576 --> 00:11:33,404
There's one back there
with Spanish written on it,

249
00:11:33,940 --> 00:11:37,060
so I'm guessing it's not
just Japanese people.

250
00:11:39,584 --> 00:11:43,002
I see the maneki-neko statue
several times a day in Japan.

251
00:11:43,002 --> 00:11:45,062
I just assumed they
were being mass produced

252
00:11:45,062 --> 00:11:47,321
in a giant cat mega factory.

253
00:11:47,662 --> 00:11:49,062
But I stumbled across a small,

254
00:11:49,087 --> 00:11:52,062
out of the way shop
which suggests otherwise.

255
00:11:54,672 --> 00:11:57,651
I never knew that a lot of these
maneki-nekos were handmade.

256
00:11:58,719 --> 00:12:00,930
You just assume they all
come off a factory line,

257
00:12:00,955 --> 00:12:03,300
but its nice seeing
them produced like this.

258
00:12:05,133 --> 00:12:06,900
Clearly, a lot of hard work
and passion

259
00:12:06,900 --> 00:12:08,069
goes into making them.

260
00:12:09,258 --> 00:12:12,100
These do look pretty beautiful.

261
00:12:12,876 --> 00:12:15,261
Look at the back, the
detail on the back as well.

262
00:12:17,660 --> 00:12:19,300
The attention to detail
and artwork

263
00:12:19,319 --> 00:12:21,192
on these statues is amazing.

264
00:12:21,192 --> 00:12:22,997
The shelves are filled
with beckoning cats

265
00:12:22,997 --> 00:12:25,571
of all breeds,
styles, and sizes.

266
00:12:25,571 --> 00:12:27,771
Perhaps, best of all,
customers can get

267
00:12:27,771 --> 00:12:30,675
their very own
personalized beckoning cats

268
00:12:30,700 --> 00:12:32,980
modeled in the likeness
of their own pet.

269
00:12:34,017 --> 00:12:35,869
So, you can actually
bring in your own cat,

270
00:12:35,869 --> 00:12:38,618
and have a cast made of it
and have it hand painted.

271
00:12:39,108 --> 00:12:41,064
So, here's a cat
that was brought in here,

272
00:12:41,462 --> 00:12:42,595
and here's the end result.

273
00:12:43,860 --> 00:12:45,626
The maneki-neko statue
isn't just believed

274
00:12:45,651 --> 00:12:47,725
to bring good
financial fortune though.

275
00:12:47,940 --> 00:12:49,552
It's also believed
to bring happiness

276
00:12:49,552 --> 00:12:51,130
in other areas of your life.

277
00:12:51,660 --> 00:12:53,460
I've learned
of a second cat temple,

278
00:12:53,470 --> 00:12:55,804
one where locals
can pray for good fortune

279
00:12:55,820 --> 00:12:57,100
in their love life.

280
00:12:57,116 --> 00:12:59,223
But first, a quick bite
and conveniently,

281
00:12:59,223 --> 00:13:03,068
there happens to be a cat
themed cafe two doors down.

282
00:13:07,180 --> 00:13:08,740
So, there's four different
types of cake here.

283
00:13:08,954 --> 00:13:11,561
They have cheesecake
down at the end,

284
00:13:12,180 --> 00:13:15,140
chocolate eclair here, a
kind of meringue over here,

285
00:13:15,157 --> 00:13:16,982
and also a cream cake
in the middle.

286
00:13:17,408 --> 00:13:20,619
They've all got little
Cate faces drawn on them.

287
00:13:25,700 --> 00:13:27,337
Just tear off one ear, shall we?

288
00:13:33,221 --> 00:13:35,043
And now, I'm gonna have
to eat the cat's face.

289
00:13:36,287 --> 00:13:37,374
Whoops.

290
00:13:38,879 --> 00:13:41,349
With my morning tea of cat
shaped cakes out of the way,

291
00:13:41,349 --> 00:13:44,292
it's time to visit our
second beckoning cat temple

292
00:13:44,292 --> 00:13:45,776
to see what we can find.

293
00:13:46,638 --> 00:13:50,471
(eclectic instrumental music)

294
00:13:54,051 --> 00:13:55,893
It looks like those are
ping pong table bats,

295
00:13:55,893 --> 00:13:59,963
but these are all wishes
that people have.

296
00:13:59,963 --> 00:14:03,016
Someone wants
to get married here quickly.

297
00:14:03,016 --> 00:14:05,791
She's decided
who she wants to marry,

298
00:14:05,791 --> 00:14:09,151
she knows who, and she wants
good fortune in her marriage.

299
00:14:09,151 --> 00:14:10,456
I feel a bit bad reading these.

300
00:14:10,456 --> 00:14:11,594
Are you supposed to read them?

301
00:14:12,300 --> 00:14:13,317
I don't know.

302
00:14:13,900 --> 00:14:15,065
"I want to get married."

303
00:14:15,454 --> 00:14:16,523
"I want a partner."

304
00:14:17,020 --> 00:14:18,239
"This year
I want to get married."

305
00:14:18,638 --> 00:14:19,897
They're all about marriage,

306
00:14:19,897 --> 00:14:20,915
they're all about dating.

307
00:14:20,940 --> 00:14:22,716
This person's
left their Apple ID.

308
00:14:25,660 --> 00:14:28,820
I don't know if that's
desperation or brilliance, but

309
00:14:29,380 --> 00:14:31,595
yeah, clearly some people
are going pretty far with this.

310
00:14:32,180 --> 00:14:33,704
I've seen email addresses
as well.

311
00:14:34,673 --> 00:14:37,055
I wonder what the God of
cats thinks about this.

312
00:14:41,613 --> 00:14:42,856
It appears I've stumbled across

313
00:14:42,856 --> 00:14:45,375
some sort of cat temple Tinder.

314
00:14:45,740 --> 00:14:47,260
Singles looking for good fortune

315
00:14:47,279 --> 00:14:49,234
and happiness in their
love lives come here

316
00:14:49,234 --> 00:14:50,991
to pray and make offerings.

317
00:14:51,030 --> 00:14:53,085
(bell sounds)

318
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:54,733
If that wasn't strange enough,

319
00:14:54,761 --> 00:14:57,821
the large cat statues inside
the shrine give this place

320
00:14:57,821 --> 00:15:01,205
the atmosphere of some
sort of cat obsessed cult.

321
00:15:02,783 --> 00:15:04,032
It's a little bit creepy
actually.

322
00:15:05,220 --> 00:15:07,953
Because there's four
giant cats waving at me,

323
00:15:08,259 --> 00:15:11,095
and then for no reason there's
a cheeky monkey down there.

324
00:15:12,514 --> 00:15:15,007
These kind of shrines are
supposed to be quite serious

325
00:15:15,069 --> 00:15:17,390
but it's a bit difficult
to take it seriously

326
00:15:17,436 --> 00:15:21,603
when you've got all this
madness staring back at you.

327
00:15:22,980 --> 00:15:24,460
And then
there's the Buddha statue,

328
00:15:24,684 --> 00:15:27,221
that yellow little Buddha statue
there.

329
00:15:28,054 --> 00:15:29,737
If these temples have
taught me anything though,

330
00:15:29,737 --> 00:15:31,827
it's that the belief in the
power of the beckoning cat

331
00:15:31,827 --> 00:15:34,709
is still very much alive and
well with Japanese culture,

332
00:15:34,940 --> 00:15:36,640
and if I ever want
to get married,

333
00:15:36,680 --> 00:15:38,675
I should scribble
my email address down

334
00:15:38,675 --> 00:15:40,232
on a ping pong racket,

335
00:15:40,232 --> 00:15:44,056
and pray to a cheeky monkey
surrounded by saluting cats.

336
00:15:44,499 --> 00:15:47,276
Well, I think that's
what I've learned anyway.

337
00:15:49,340 --> 00:15:50,570
What's going on there?

338
00:15:50,990 --> 00:15:53,441
(bright singing)

339
00:15:53,738 --> 00:15:55,905
There's like some people
dancing in front of the shrine.

340
00:15:58,300 --> 00:15:59,480
Oh my lord.

341
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:03,837
(singing in Japanese)

342
00:16:05,895 --> 00:16:07,664
It's creepy, it's like
some sort of cat cult

343
00:16:07,664 --> 00:16:09,084
with the cats in the background.

344
00:16:13,220 --> 00:16:14,700
I find this really hard
to take seriously

345
00:16:14,711 --> 00:16:16,750
because I'm not
a superstitious man,

346
00:16:16,750 --> 00:16:19,392
and then to see them dancing
in front of the cat shrine

347
00:16:21,690 --> 00:16:24,790
doing the most ridiculous dance
I've ever seen in my life.

348
00:16:24,790 --> 00:16:26,470
I can't take it seriously.

349
00:16:26,533 --> 00:16:27,533
(laughs)

350
00:16:29,124 --> 00:16:31,166
Still, if all this cat
superstition

351
00:16:31,218 --> 00:16:32,383
seems hard to believe,

352
00:16:32,412 --> 00:16:34,181
I'm about to have
my beliefs questioned

353
00:16:34,181 --> 00:16:36,503
by one of Japan's
most famous cats.

354
00:16:37,739 --> 00:16:40,684
I'm on my way to a small
town an hour north of Tokyo

355
00:16:40,684 --> 00:16:42,966
to meet a cat
I've read about in the news,

356
00:16:42,966 --> 00:16:45,166
and seen on TV numerous times.

357
00:16:45,191 --> 00:16:47,507
The cat who has allegedly
brought considerable wealth

358
00:16:47,546 --> 00:16:50,879
to the locals, thanks
in part to its lucky eyebrows.

359
00:16:51,026 --> 00:16:52,146
And no, I'm not joking,

360
00:16:52,146 --> 00:16:54,303
these are some pretty
ground breaking eyebrows.

361
00:16:57,582 --> 00:17:00,161
Meet Hachi,
the luckiest cat in Japan.

362
00:17:00,438 --> 00:17:02,527
Hachi works at a tobacco shop,

363
00:17:02,527 --> 00:17:05,119
which also happens to
sell lottery tickets.

364
00:17:05,420 --> 00:17:07,700
The shop has had a string
of jackpot winners,

365
00:17:07,805 --> 00:17:09,842
and many winners
attribute their success

366
00:17:09,842 --> 00:17:12,430
to the good fortune
and presence of Hachi.

367
00:17:13,440 --> 00:17:15,305
This cat has got
quite the reception.

368
00:17:16,860 --> 00:17:18,481
The cat's called Hachi,

369
00:17:18,521 --> 00:17:20,592
and Hachi
is the number eight in Japanese,

370
00:17:20,592 --> 00:17:22,387
and eight is a lucky number,

371
00:17:22,387 --> 00:17:26,554
so the symbol for eight
in kanji a lucky number,

372
00:17:26,900 --> 00:17:30,499
and hence the cat is good luck.

373
00:17:30,524 --> 00:17:32,398
And you can see here
how many times

374
00:17:32,398 --> 00:17:35,086
people have won the
lottery in recent times.

375
00:17:35,685 --> 00:17:38,141
According to these signs
outside the front of the shop,

376
00:17:38,141 --> 00:17:41,445
good fortune is exactly
what Hachi has brought.

377
00:17:41,445 --> 00:17:42,722
Well, if not by the winnings,

378
00:17:42,722 --> 00:17:44,925
then certainly by all the
pilgrimages people have made

379
00:17:44,925 --> 00:17:47,461
from around the country
to see the famous cat

380
00:17:47,461 --> 00:17:49,034
with the lucky eyebrows.

381
00:17:50,060 --> 00:17:51,838
I was given the cat
from a friend

382
00:17:51,860 --> 00:17:55,850
and it had this unique pattern
on its face.

383
00:17:56,260 --> 00:18:01,300
I knew the lady who
runs the tobacco store

384
00:18:01,325 --> 00:18:04,435
and because I'm not around
during the day,

385
00:18:04,460 --> 00:18:07,156
I asked her to take care
of my cat.

386
00:18:07,860 --> 00:18:13,620
Little by little, word of Hachi
and her unusual color spread

387
00:18:13,734 --> 00:18:16,875
and she became very popular.

388
00:18:18,808 --> 00:18:21,075
In Japanese,
this pattern resembles

389
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:24,060
the character for
the number eight,

390
00:18:24,220 --> 00:18:28,202
which is said to be
a lucky number.

391
00:18:29,333 --> 00:18:31,505
This is a list of people
who have won recently.

392
00:18:31,867 --> 00:18:34,677
And you can see here someone
has won 14 million yen.

393
00:18:35,138 --> 00:18:37,421
It says here,
(speaking Japanese)

394
00:18:37,928 --> 00:18:39,507
"The next winner could be you."

395
00:18:40,864 --> 00:18:42,952
He did have quite the
audience a few minutes ago.

396
00:18:42,952 --> 00:18:44,397
There were about
half a dozen people

397
00:18:44,397 --> 00:18:46,162
standing here taking pictures,

398
00:18:46,162 --> 00:18:48,658
but clearly he got a bit tired,

399
00:18:48,658 --> 00:18:50,593
and decided to go back in now.

400
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:53,660
It's not easy being a cat
working at a tobacco store.

401
00:18:55,042 --> 00:18:56,419
(meowing)

402
00:18:56,580 --> 00:18:59,028
Hachi may be
the luckiest cat in Japan,

403
00:18:59,059 --> 00:19:01,671
but by no means
the only cat with a job.

404
00:19:02,340 --> 00:19:04,500
Unlike the lazy cats
we have in the west,

405
00:19:04,539 --> 00:19:07,715
it seems some Japanese
cats aren't satisfied

406
00:19:07,740 --> 00:19:09,235
with simply
lying about the house

407
00:19:09,260 --> 00:19:10,994
knocking photos off the shelves.

408
00:19:11,220 --> 00:19:13,613
Some of them
like to earn a living.

409
00:19:14,100 --> 00:19:15,995
The most unusual case
I've heard about

410
00:19:16,020 --> 00:19:17,755
comes from a small train station

411
00:19:17,780 --> 00:19:19,780
in a rural town in East Japan.

412
00:19:20,380 --> 00:19:21,980
Naturally,
when I first heard about

413
00:19:21,984 --> 00:19:23,935
a train station run by a cat,

414
00:19:23,935 --> 00:19:26,069
I assumed my ears were broken.

415
00:19:26,620 --> 00:19:28,780
Fortunately, it turned out
they weren't.

416
00:19:31,580 --> 00:19:33,515
This is actually
a normal, regular train

417
00:19:33,540 --> 00:19:36,140
that people catch everyday to
go to work, to go to school.

418
00:19:36,940 --> 00:19:39,360
When it feels like
something out of Disneyland.

419
00:19:42,100 --> 00:19:43,835
There's cat things everywhere.

420
00:19:43,860 --> 00:19:47,720
There's Doraemon, arguably
Japan's most famous

421
00:19:47,745 --> 00:19:48,860
cat character here.

422
00:19:50,574 --> 00:19:51,595
It's locked.

423
00:19:51,620 --> 00:19:53,740
There's a cat library,
cat books here.

424
00:19:55,826 --> 00:19:57,039
Don't know what that is.

425
00:19:59,100 --> 00:20:00,475
"I've studied many philosophers,

426
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:03,530
many cats, the wisdom of
cats is infinitely superior."

427
00:20:04,540 --> 00:20:05,700
It's the premise of this book.

428
00:20:06,020 --> 00:20:08,620
"Everything I know about
life I learned from my cat."

429
00:20:09,710 --> 00:20:11,960
When I heard
it was a cat themed train,

430
00:20:12,380 --> 00:20:14,660
I just pictured some stickers
on the wall or something.

431
00:20:14,980 --> 00:20:17,392
I didn't think the whole
interior would feel like,

432
00:20:18,353 --> 00:20:19,401
well, like this.

433
00:20:20,060 --> 00:20:22,620
A library, some cabinets,

434
00:20:23,700 --> 00:20:26,353
and special sofas built into it.

435
00:20:26,900 --> 00:20:29,725
Right, this is
a genuine cat themed train.

436
00:20:31,740 --> 00:20:34,460
This cat themed train is
a spectacle in itself.

437
00:20:34,940 --> 00:20:37,715
We're riding it to Kishi
Station in Wakayama Prefecture

438
00:20:37,740 --> 00:20:40,060
to meet the cat train
station master,

439
00:20:40,300 --> 00:20:42,380
and find out what led
the locals to convert

440
00:20:42,386 --> 00:20:45,937
a standard train into a
cat themed wonderland.

441
00:20:46,016 --> 00:20:47,696
(train engine whirrs)

442
00:20:47,773 --> 00:20:49,373
(indistinct chatter)

443
00:20:49,889 --> 00:20:50,917
Wow.

444
00:20:52,061 --> 00:20:54,914
Nitama, the station master cat.

445
00:20:57,460 --> 00:20:59,500
And it's got quite the audience.

446
00:21:00,500 --> 00:21:03,780
There's about a dozen
people surrounding the cat,

447
00:21:03,798 --> 00:21:05,020
and taking pictures.

448
00:21:06,940 --> 00:21:09,780
It's looks completely oblivious
to everyone standing here.

449
00:21:10,185 --> 00:21:14,064
(laughing)
It just doesn't care.

450
00:21:16,120 --> 00:21:19,322
It says here,
on 22nd of June, 2015,

451
00:21:19,322 --> 00:21:22,035
Tama passed away
and became an honorable

452
00:21:22,060 --> 00:21:24,420
eternal station master.

453
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:27,180
So, the cat
is still here in spirit.

454
00:21:27,860 --> 00:21:29,755
Because that's not enough to
contribute to the economy,

455
00:21:29,780 --> 00:21:31,700
they've got a second cat,
Nitama, here.

456
00:21:33,220 --> 00:21:35,251
Apparently, the cats
have contributed

457
00:21:35,300 --> 00:21:37,795
over 10 million dollars
to the local economy

458
00:21:37,820 --> 00:21:39,949
just by sheer number of
tourists coming here.

459
00:21:40,740 --> 00:21:44,877
It also says here that Nitama
has regular working hours

460
00:21:45,540 --> 00:21:46,877
like other employees.

461
00:21:47,340 --> 00:21:50,862
She usually works except
for Wednesday and Thursday

462
00:21:51,180 --> 00:21:52,455
because that's her day off.

463
00:21:53,784 --> 00:21:57,555
In the past, Kishi Station was
a small unremarkable station

464
00:21:57,580 --> 00:21:59,388
out here in rural Japan.

465
00:21:59,818 --> 00:22:01,635
But since the induction of Tama,

466
00:22:01,660 --> 00:22:03,395
the original station master cat,

467
00:22:03,513 --> 00:22:05,513
and her successor, Nitama,

468
00:22:05,620 --> 00:22:08,594
both the station and the
local economy have flourished.

469
00:22:08,940 --> 00:22:12,060
Once again, cats hare bringing
good fortune to their owners.

470
00:22:12,071 --> 00:22:13,527
Maybe there is something to this

471
00:22:13,527 --> 00:22:15,944
good luck cat idea after all.

472
00:22:16,587 --> 00:22:19,076
(playful instrumental music)
(camera shutter clicks)

473
00:22:19,100 --> 00:22:21,613
So, they brought the cat
out, put a hat on it,

474
00:22:22,347 --> 00:22:24,395
and about 50 people just
magically appeared

475
00:22:24,420 --> 00:22:26,089
out of nowhere,
there was no one here.

476
00:22:26,433 --> 00:22:29,698
And now, many,
many pictures being taken.

477
00:22:30,940 --> 00:22:32,651
I just love
how the cat's so oblivious.

478
00:22:32,967 --> 00:22:35,097
The cat's just like,
"What is going on?"

479
00:22:35,860 --> 00:22:36,967
I love the hat.

480
00:22:37,950 --> 00:22:40,295
I think all cats
should have a hat,

481
00:22:40,295 --> 00:22:42,740
and look, it just fits
perfectly, it looks wonderful.

482
00:22:43,380 --> 00:22:44,860
He's a rather dashing cat.

483
00:22:45,380 --> 00:22:47,060
The cat seems to like it.

484
00:22:51,060 --> 00:22:54,700
It's remarkable,
all you've you gotta do:

485
00:22:54,735 --> 00:22:58,627
stick a tiny hat on a cat...

486
00:22:58,980 --> 00:23:00,460
This is the result.

487
00:23:02,140 --> 00:23:04,060
If there's anyone
in Detroit watching,

488
00:23:04,080 --> 00:23:05,950
your city
crumbling in on itself,

489
00:23:06,559 --> 00:23:09,293
get some cats and just have
them run around Detroit,

490
00:23:09,319 --> 00:23:11,520
stick some hats on them,
people will come.

491
00:23:11,520 --> 00:23:13,030
The economy will go back up.

492
00:23:18,764 --> 00:23:20,575
Nitama is the second cat
to be named

493
00:23:20,575 --> 00:23:22,672
the station master of Kishi.

494
00:23:22,993 --> 00:23:25,345
Sadly, Tama,
the first station master,

495
00:23:25,540 --> 00:23:27,740
passed away in 2015.

496
00:23:28,140 --> 00:23:29,940
And locals now
come to the station

497
00:23:29,951 --> 00:23:31,784
to pay their respects.

498
00:23:33,282 --> 00:23:34,722
When Tama passed away,

499
00:23:35,380 --> 00:23:37,142
3,000 people turned up
for the funeral

500
00:23:37,167 --> 00:23:39,370
when it was a traditional
Japanese funeral,

501
00:23:39,370 --> 00:23:41,809
it was a big deal
and this is the shrine.

502
00:23:43,580 --> 00:23:48,077
The cat is now an honorable
goddess of the station,

503
00:23:48,580 --> 00:23:51,640
and now you can come here
and pray to her

504
00:23:52,460 --> 00:23:54,282
whilst watching out
for wasps and bees.

505
00:23:56,600 --> 00:23:57,679
Lovely.

506
00:23:57,711 --> 00:24:01,878
(upbeat instrumental music)

507
00:24:02,100 --> 00:24:03,740
After seeing
the impressive wealth

508
00:24:03,742 --> 00:24:06,056
a few cats have brought
not just to individuals,

509
00:24:06,056 --> 00:24:08,082
but to entire local economies,

510
00:24:08,082 --> 00:24:10,555
and country side towns,
and remote islands.

511
00:24:10,780 --> 00:24:12,300
I'm starting to think
I need to buy

512
00:24:12,315 --> 00:24:13,987
some cats for myself.

513
00:24:14,220 --> 00:24:16,515
And what better place
for me to sit and reflect

514
00:24:16,540 --> 00:24:18,896
on some sort of cutting edge
business plan

515
00:24:18,940 --> 00:24:20,380
then at a cat pub,

516
00:24:20,420 --> 00:24:24,052
a Japanese businessman's
equivalent to a cat cafe.

517
00:24:25,020 --> 00:24:27,235
So, this is a cat izakaya.

518
00:24:27,260 --> 00:24:30,435
It says here,
(speaking Japanese)

519
00:24:30,460 --> 00:24:32,743
so, "A place where you
can play with cats."

520
00:24:34,660 --> 00:24:35,766
But it's also a pub.

521
00:24:36,500 --> 00:24:37,610
Let's go and check it out.

522
00:24:40,060 --> 00:24:42,128
And there's quite a lot
of cats on the door.

523
00:24:42,420 --> 00:24:43,503
So, that's a giveaway.

524
00:24:44,420 --> 00:24:47,540
There's a cat on top of
the stairs welcoming us.

525
00:24:49,657 --> 00:24:53,407
(playful instrumental music)

526
00:24:58,540 --> 00:24:59,915
Even the cats at the pub

527
00:24:59,940 --> 00:25:02,715
look like they've lapped
up a few pints of sake,

528
00:25:02,740 --> 00:25:04,515
slumped over
the chairs at the bar,

529
00:25:04,540 --> 00:25:07,220
presumably after
a hard day at work.

530
00:25:12,587 --> 00:25:14,136
It's certainly a much
more relaxing atmosphere

531
00:25:14,136 --> 00:25:15,469
than a cat cafe.

532
00:25:23,067 --> 00:25:26,977
It feels a bit weird sitting
at a bar with your beer,

533
00:25:26,977 --> 00:25:28,544
and half a dozen cats
around you.

534
00:25:29,641 --> 00:25:30,676
I like it though.

535
00:25:30,780 --> 00:25:31,850
They've got their biscuits,

536
00:25:31,882 --> 00:25:33,090
I've got my nuts.

537
00:25:33,090 --> 00:25:34,274
Everyone's a winner.

538
00:25:34,274 --> 00:25:35,734
A standard Friday night.

539
00:25:36,820 --> 00:25:39,420
Beer on tap,
shattered businessmen,

540
00:25:39,740 --> 00:25:42,258
and an abundance of cats
all in one room.

541
00:25:42,633 --> 00:25:44,492
What could possibly go wrong?

542
00:25:46,300 --> 00:25:48,495
Customers sit here drinking

543
00:25:48,520 --> 00:25:52,199
and a cat will walk by
and step in their drink.

544
00:25:52,591 --> 00:25:53,698
(laughs)
Oh no.

545
00:25:54,956 --> 00:25:57,555
So apparently, sometimes the
customers are sitting here

546
00:25:57,580 --> 00:25:58,980
drinking their beer,
the cat comes along,

547
00:25:58,998 --> 00:26:01,595
and accidentally sticks
its paw in the drink,

548
00:26:01,620 --> 00:26:02,748
and then walks off,

549
00:26:03,260 --> 00:26:05,202
so they have to throw the
drink away and start again.

550
00:26:06,180 --> 00:26:08,710
It's not easy
running a cat pub (laughs).

551
00:26:11,420 --> 00:26:13,460
So, why did you start
having all the cats here?

552
00:26:13,478 --> 00:26:15,318
What was your reason
for having the cats

553
00:26:15,318 --> 00:26:16,622
here in the first place?

554
00:26:17,380 --> 00:26:19,780
I opened this bar
around six years ago

555
00:26:19,863 --> 00:26:21,930
but not so many customers came.

556
00:26:22,980 --> 00:26:24,784
But there was one customer

557
00:26:24,824 --> 00:26:27,735
whose cat had
a litter of kittens.

558
00:26:28,500 --> 00:26:30,500
The customer didn't know what to
do with them

559
00:26:30,561 --> 00:26:32,889
so I offered to adopt them,

560
00:26:32,921 --> 00:26:35,521
and the number of cats
grew from there.

561
00:26:37,460 --> 00:26:40,260
Just like all izakayas,
this one serves food.

562
00:26:40,262 --> 00:26:43,959
So, for relaxing times,
make it Suntory time.

563
00:26:43,959 --> 00:26:47,360
Oh, and throw in a cat
faced pasta along the way.

564
00:26:48,896 --> 00:26:51,995
Yeah, it's a little bit
weird to drink alcohol

565
00:26:52,020 --> 00:26:55,300
in the presence of many
many cats like this.

566
00:26:58,780 --> 00:27:00,960
Having a drink
and playing with a cat.

567
00:27:01,546 --> 00:27:03,304
Two things that go hand in hand.

568
00:27:04,587 --> 00:27:08,569
(laughing)

569
00:27:09,772 --> 00:27:12,235
Cats in a bar actually
makes a lot more sense

570
00:27:12,260 --> 00:27:13,260
than I expected.

571
00:27:13,298 --> 00:27:14,348
For the lonely drinker,

572
00:27:14,348 --> 00:27:17,240
they prove to be ideal
company and entertainment

573
00:27:17,240 --> 00:27:18,552
all rolled into one.

574
00:27:20,100 --> 00:27:23,922
(eclectic instrumental music)

575
00:27:24,020 --> 00:27:25,058
Just doing a bit of research

576
00:27:25,083 --> 00:27:27,242
on weird cat stuff in Japan,

577
00:27:27,693 --> 00:27:29,082
and I found this cat
that regularly

578
00:27:29,082 --> 00:27:31,247
rides the train through Tokyo,

579
00:27:31,247 --> 00:27:33,924
and sits with the passengers.

580
00:27:34,100 --> 00:27:36,035
I'd quite like to try
and track this cat down,

581
00:27:36,060 --> 00:27:39,075
but it's on the Ikebukuro line,

582
00:27:39,100 --> 00:27:41,765
and Ikebukuro has the fifth
biggest station in the world,

583
00:27:41,820 --> 00:27:44,420
so... still you never
know your luck, one day.

584
00:27:46,380 --> 00:27:49,875
Finding this elusive commuter
cat would be near impossible

585
00:27:49,900 --> 00:27:52,660
given the sheer size of
Tokyo's train network.

586
00:27:52,900 --> 00:27:54,540
But fortunately,
cats can also be found

587
00:27:54,554 --> 00:27:57,447
in a few other obscure
public places.

588
00:27:58,340 --> 00:28:00,220
One such place is Hibiya Park,

589
00:28:00,267 --> 00:28:03,051
located right next to
the Imperial Palace.

590
00:28:05,580 --> 00:28:07,540
I've heard it has
a reputation of being

591
00:28:07,574 --> 00:28:09,791
something
of an unofficial cat park

592
00:28:09,791 --> 00:28:13,086
due the the numerous feral
cats that call it home.

593
00:28:14,420 --> 00:28:17,555
Cat lazying around over
there behind the roses.

594
00:28:18,101 --> 00:28:19,841
I thought it was a pile of sand,

595
00:28:20,060 --> 00:28:21,811
but nope, it is a cat.

596
00:28:22,343 --> 00:28:24,780
(funky instrumental music)

597
00:28:26,231 --> 00:28:29,230
Spotting cats in this massive
park can be quite tricky.

598
00:28:29,540 --> 00:28:31,075
There isn't
an abundance of them,

599
00:28:31,100 --> 00:28:33,595
but with some persistence
and a bit of luck,

600
00:28:33,620 --> 00:28:36,252
cat sightings
are certainly possible.

601
00:28:40,162 --> 00:28:41,635
Similar to Hibiya Park,

602
00:28:41,660 --> 00:28:44,115
a large cemetery
in suburban Tokyo

603
00:28:44,140 --> 00:28:46,475
has been nicknamed
the cat cemetery

604
00:28:46,500 --> 00:28:48,747
on account of its
numerous strays.

605
00:28:49,630 --> 00:28:51,794
(funky instrumental music)

606
00:28:53,660 --> 00:28:55,260
I must admit,
I wasn't optimistic

607
00:28:55,269 --> 00:28:56,740
we were gonna find cats here,

608
00:28:57,460 --> 00:29:00,460
and we walked straight in and
the first two minutes, a cat.

609
00:29:01,580 --> 00:29:03,096
This lovely cat shows up.

610
00:29:07,312 --> 00:29:10,969
(playful instrumental music)

611
00:29:13,780 --> 00:29:15,835
The tight spaces
and concrete sprawl

612
00:29:15,860 --> 00:29:17,395
of this massive graveyard,

613
00:29:17,420 --> 00:29:20,420
make for the ideal playground
for the feral cats.

614
00:29:21,245 --> 00:29:23,073
(playful instrumental music)

615
00:29:26,060 --> 00:29:27,263
It's like a game
of hide and seek.

616
00:29:27,380 --> 00:29:29,755
He... pops up and goes, "Meow!"

617
00:29:29,780 --> 00:29:31,780
And then runs away and
hides around the corner.

618
00:29:32,540 --> 00:29:33,951
And then meows again,
and looks at me.

619
00:29:34,099 --> 00:29:35,809
(meowing)
Like that.

620
00:29:35,942 --> 00:29:38,163
(laughing)

621
00:29:38,163 --> 00:29:39,623
Moving onto his next spot.

622
00:29:41,252 --> 00:29:45,002
(playful instrumental music)

623
00:29:45,350 --> 00:29:46,350
Oh!

624
00:29:47,246 --> 00:29:49,248
It's getting heated.
(meowing)

625
00:29:49,940 --> 00:29:51,380
Awe, it's gonna be a fight.

626
00:29:51,580 --> 00:29:54,635
These two cats seem to have
some sort of little gang going,

627
00:29:54,660 --> 00:29:56,660
and this one's
not invited to the party.

628
00:29:59,380 --> 00:30:01,220
I feel sorry for this black cat.

629
00:30:01,620 --> 00:30:03,133
He's been very much excluded.

630
00:30:03,172 --> 00:30:05,835
The other two cats seems
to be sort of best friends.

631
00:30:05,860 --> 00:30:07,977
This cat has to
keep his distance,

632
00:30:08,300 --> 00:30:10,820
and you know, I feel a
little bit sympathetic.

633
00:30:12,020 --> 00:30:13,794
It reminds me
of my old school days.

634
00:30:15,621 --> 00:30:17,230
(recoils) Ew!

635
00:30:19,901 --> 00:30:20,937
(laughing)

636
00:30:20,962 --> 00:30:22,018
Oh no.

637
00:30:22,043 --> 00:30:23,058
I was leaning on that,

638
00:30:23,083 --> 00:30:25,373
and then I looked down and
there's like 20 red ants.

639
00:30:31,180 --> 00:30:33,460
A cat cemetery
may not be overrun,

640
00:30:33,468 --> 00:30:35,574
but it's not difficult
to stumble across them

641
00:30:35,574 --> 00:30:36,853
whilst strolling around.

642
00:30:39,436 --> 00:30:41,669
The cemetery
also backs onto a district

643
00:30:41,669 --> 00:30:44,995
called Yanaka Ginza,
where supposedly,

644
00:30:45,020 --> 00:30:46,900
the locals are very cat friendly

645
00:30:47,260 --> 00:30:49,940
adopting a few strays
as community mascots,

646
00:30:49,947 --> 00:30:52,265
and building shelters
and litter boxes

647
00:30:52,620 --> 00:30:54,100
throughout the street.

648
00:30:56,380 --> 00:30:59,500
So, this is Yanaka Ginza
suburb or street,

649
00:30:59,517 --> 00:31:02,877
and apparently, again, it's
got a famous reputation

650
00:31:02,877 --> 00:31:04,850
for being a cat friendly
neighborhood,

651
00:31:05,364 --> 00:31:07,068
and it's right next to
the cemetery,

652
00:31:07,820 --> 00:31:10,515
so I'm guessing it lives
up to its reputation

653
00:31:10,540 --> 00:31:12,180
especially as we've already seen
one cat

654
00:31:12,820 --> 00:31:15,260
just relaxing at the side
of the street a minute ago.

655
00:31:15,820 --> 00:31:17,100
We've got two
statues of cats here

656
00:31:17,114 --> 00:31:21,281
next to this big giant ice
cream cone, the beckoning cat.

657
00:31:22,878 --> 00:31:24,312
There's a lot of cat symbols,

658
00:31:24,312 --> 00:31:25,967
and statues and things.

659
00:31:25,967 --> 00:31:27,584
There's a cat
on the roof up there.

660
00:31:28,177 --> 00:31:30,379
I thought it was real
out the corner of my eye,

661
00:31:30,379 --> 00:31:33,256
but no, it's not real.

662
00:31:34,140 --> 00:31:36,874
It's rather terrifying
as well (laughs).

663
00:31:39,260 --> 00:31:40,300
As the day moves on,

664
00:31:40,324 --> 00:31:42,315
and more and more
shoppers arrive,

665
00:31:42,500 --> 00:31:43,820
the neighborhood comes alive

666
00:31:43,837 --> 00:31:46,053
with all manner
of cat appreciation.

667
00:31:46,660 --> 00:31:50,850
Cat merchandise, cat
statues, cat shaped food.

668
00:31:51,580 --> 00:31:52,940
You can hardly move
down the street

669
00:31:52,956 --> 00:31:56,299
without bumping into something
with a cat stuck on it.

670
00:31:56,623 --> 00:32:00,240
(playful instrumental music)

671
00:32:07,657 --> 00:32:09,738
A lot of savvy business
owners in Japan

672
00:32:09,738 --> 00:32:12,290
have seen the marketing
appeal of cats.

673
00:32:12,712 --> 00:32:14,609
Need to draw
some customers to your pub?

674
00:32:14,860 --> 00:32:16,193
Add some cats.

675
00:32:16,740 --> 00:32:19,875
Want instant tourism for
a small rural community?

676
00:32:19,900 --> 00:32:22,552
Put a hat on a cat
and make her the boss.

677
00:32:23,020 --> 00:32:25,275
There's even a politician
who nominated

678
00:32:25,300 --> 00:32:26,875
a cat as his running mate.

679
00:32:27,766 --> 00:32:30,555
But for the owner of this
bookstore in Central Tokyo,

680
00:32:30,820 --> 00:32:32,695
adding a cat or two
wasn't enough.

681
00:32:33,300 --> 00:32:35,915
So, he decided to
overhaul his entire store

682
00:32:35,940 --> 00:32:38,780
selling nothing
but cat related books.

683
00:32:38,980 --> 00:32:40,540
What a way to stand out.

684
00:32:41,780 --> 00:32:42,870
This is a famous cat.

685
00:32:43,667 --> 00:32:45,272
He blows bubbles
out of his nose.

686
00:32:49,612 --> 00:32:53,595
To say that there's a lot of
cat related books and products

687
00:32:53,820 --> 00:32:55,020
is quite the understatement.

688
00:32:55,380 --> 00:32:56,860
There's a ridiculous amount.

689
00:32:57,626 --> 00:32:58,949
The Islands of Greece.

690
00:33:00,700 --> 00:33:04,300
And it's just the Islands of
Greece with lots of cats in.

691
00:33:07,126 --> 00:33:08,964
Everything from cat
coloring books

692
00:33:08,964 --> 00:33:12,515
to philosophy
as interpreted by cats.

693
00:33:12,540 --> 00:33:14,915
How the owner managed
to fill an entire store

694
00:33:14,940 --> 00:33:17,835
with this just cat related
books is remarkable.

695
00:33:17,860 --> 00:33:20,115
If cat enthusiasts had a heaven,

696
00:33:20,140 --> 00:33:21,900
this would be its library.

697
00:33:23,420 --> 00:33:26,722
This book sums up Japan's
cat obsession rather well.

698
00:33:27,707 --> 00:33:30,379
It's got all the data on the
most popular types of cats.

699
00:33:30,740 --> 00:33:35,251
It's even got a section on the
different types of cat legs

700
00:33:35,751 --> 00:33:38,125
just in case you ever
needed to know that.

701
00:33:38,807 --> 00:33:41,007
(indistinct
background chatter)

702
00:33:41,580 --> 00:33:43,729
Different types of cat smile.

703
00:33:44,510 --> 00:33:47,257
This is a book about cats in
funny positions and places.

704
00:33:48,023 --> 00:33:49,209
Let's see.

705
00:33:49,694 --> 00:33:51,507
It's like Mission
Impossible cat.

706
00:33:52,862 --> 00:33:55,694
Surprisingly, or
unsurprisingly, to be honest,

707
00:33:55,700 --> 00:33:57,155
I'm not sure which,

708
00:33:57,180 --> 00:33:59,715
converting the entire
store to cat only books

709
00:33:59,740 --> 00:34:01,660
has increased it's popularity.

710
00:34:02,020 --> 00:34:04,900
The cat's good fortune
has struck again.

711
00:34:05,700 --> 00:34:08,841
I've had this store
for about 35 years.

712
00:34:08,883 --> 00:34:11,923
It seems the younger generation

713
00:34:11,948 --> 00:34:13,718
doesn't read books anymore.

714
00:34:13,743 --> 00:34:15,962
So to combat this,

715
00:34:15,987 --> 00:34:18,453
I converted
what was a regular book store

716
00:34:18,478 --> 00:34:21,375
into a cat book store.

717
00:34:21,415 --> 00:34:25,498
Since then, I've seen
a steady increase in customers.

718
00:34:27,380 --> 00:34:29,674
This is the most popular
kind of book they sell here.

719
00:34:30,221 --> 00:34:32,423
It's cats wearing
different items

720
00:34:32,423 --> 00:34:34,668
or just like in these
really funny situations

721
00:34:34,668 --> 00:34:37,221
where it looks like they're
having an amazing time.

722
00:34:38,378 --> 00:34:41,628
"Don't expect a lucky break
to just fall from the sky,"

723
00:34:42,151 --> 00:34:43,267
and the cat's looking up.

724
00:34:44,300 --> 00:34:46,420
"To think as if
the reverse is true."

725
00:34:48,700 --> 00:34:50,540
"Negativity prohibited."

726
00:34:51,500 --> 00:34:53,100
They're sayings,
everyday sayings,

727
00:34:53,860 --> 00:34:55,140
with the cat acting it out.

728
00:34:55,780 --> 00:34:58,260
"The longer you wait,
the better it tastes."

729
00:34:58,506 --> 00:35:01,389
(laughing)
I like that one.

730
00:35:02,502 --> 00:35:06,169
(upbeat instrumental music)

731
00:35:08,780 --> 00:35:10,620
It has become apparent
that cats can be found

732
00:35:10,630 --> 00:35:13,024
in some pretty
unconventional places.

733
00:35:13,220 --> 00:35:16,235
But this next place is surely
near the top of the list.

734
00:35:16,660 --> 00:35:18,355
I'm going in search
of a business,

735
00:35:18,380 --> 00:35:20,915
which utilizes
the presence of cats

736
00:35:20,940 --> 00:35:22,820
to boost staff morale,

737
00:35:22,900 --> 00:35:25,750
and create a fun, friendly
office environment.

738
00:35:26,260 --> 00:35:29,420
But can cats in an
office space really work?

739
00:35:31,500 --> 00:35:34,515
This is the office
of Ferray Corporation,

740
00:35:34,540 --> 00:35:36,155
an e-commerce company.

741
00:35:36,180 --> 00:35:38,115
Here in this place of business,

742
00:35:38,140 --> 00:35:40,155
cats are allowed to roam free,

743
00:35:40,180 --> 00:35:43,875
pouncing on computer mice,
strolling across keyboards,

744
00:35:43,900 --> 00:35:47,295
and of course, nibbling their
way through computer cables.

745
00:35:48,069 --> 00:35:50,650
But what happens when
the male and female cats

746
00:35:50,860 --> 00:35:53,220
start to look at each
other longingly?

747
00:35:53,230 --> 00:35:56,242
To stop the cats from completely
tearing the office apart

748
00:35:56,420 --> 00:35:58,556
some precautions have been made.

749
00:35:59,380 --> 00:36:01,020
The female cats are upstairs

750
00:36:01,034 --> 00:36:03,014
and the male cats
are downstairs.

751
00:36:03,039 --> 00:36:05,653
The male and female cats
don't get along

752
00:36:05,678 --> 00:36:07,406
so we keep them separate.

753
00:36:08,926 --> 00:36:10,926
So, the cats in the office
have different owners,

754
00:36:10,951 --> 00:36:13,026
so the staff can bring
their cats here.

755
00:36:13,965 --> 00:36:16,399
So, the cats aren't all
owned by the office.

756
00:36:16,465 --> 00:36:18,756
It's staff coming and
bringing their cats to work.

757
00:36:19,940 --> 00:36:21,380
So, what was your thinking

758
00:36:21,486 --> 00:36:23,633
behind having
cats in the office?

759
00:36:24,740 --> 00:36:27,199
We've had cats
from the very beginning

760
00:36:28,660 --> 00:36:30,241
and the number of cats
has kept growing.

761
00:36:31,340 --> 00:36:33,500
We work with computers every day

762
00:36:33,535 --> 00:36:36,184
and the staff
all keep to themselves

763
00:36:36,620 --> 00:36:40,285
but having the cats creates
conversation in the office.

764
00:36:41,980 --> 00:36:44,155
Do you ever find
cats get in the way

765
00:36:44,180 --> 00:36:46,727
and disrupt work in the office?

766
00:36:46,900 --> 00:36:48,660
Sometimes a cat will

767
00:36:48,705 --> 00:36:51,127
cut off a customer's phone call

768
00:36:51,500 --> 00:36:55,135
or meow during a conversation,

769
00:36:55,420 --> 00:36:57,934
and the cats frequently stomp
on keyboards.

770
00:37:05,450 --> 00:37:06,982
It's not all good having
cats in your office.

771
00:37:07,820 --> 00:37:08,898
These ear phones

772
00:37:09,860 --> 00:37:11,682
Have met their demise.
(laughing)

773
00:37:12,695 --> 00:37:14,695
At the hands of one of the cats.

774
00:37:16,633 --> 00:37:20,155
So, these bits of plastic
here on top of the computers

775
00:37:20,180 --> 00:37:22,540
are to stop cats from
treading on the power buttons.

776
00:37:23,015 --> 00:37:24,871
Apparently cats
were just coming over,

777
00:37:24,871 --> 00:37:26,687
and just standing
on all the buttons.

778
00:37:27,500 --> 00:37:29,675
The cats help
to create a casual,

779
00:37:29,700 --> 00:37:31,740
stress free environment
for the staff,

780
00:37:31,780 --> 00:37:33,715
which is quite a change
from the usual

781
00:37:33,740 --> 00:37:36,755
high pressure office
environments found in Japan.

782
00:37:37,333 --> 00:37:39,323
Plus, it's certainly
a great way for owners

783
00:37:39,323 --> 00:37:42,727
who work long hours to spend
more time with their cats.

784
00:37:43,922 --> 00:37:46,080
But how to get them
safely to and from work

785
00:37:46,080 --> 00:37:48,365
on the world's
busiest subway trains?

786
00:37:49,140 --> 00:37:51,355
Well, say hello
to the custom made

787
00:37:51,380 --> 00:37:53,586
urban cat transportation device.

788
00:37:57,023 --> 00:37:58,199
Oh, I like this.

789
00:37:59,900 --> 00:38:00,983
Very stylish.

790
00:38:02,871 --> 00:38:05,269
So, he's going home for the day,

791
00:38:06,254 --> 00:38:08,255
and taking the cat
with him in style.

792
00:38:08,255 --> 00:38:11,115
(laughing)

793
00:38:11,140 --> 00:38:13,108
I've never seen
a bag quite like it.

794
00:38:13,764 --> 00:38:15,181
Cat themed merchandise
can be found

795
00:38:15,206 --> 00:38:17,595
at many retail stores
across Japan

796
00:38:17,620 --> 00:38:20,580
although usually, it's limited
to stationary and clothing.

797
00:38:20,581 --> 00:38:24,075
Although, specialized cat
products like the cat carry bag

798
00:38:24,100 --> 00:38:25,740
are available
if you look hard enough.

799
00:38:26,580 --> 00:38:27,900
But some gift stores have taken

800
00:38:27,911 --> 00:38:30,239
their love of cat products
to new heights.

801
00:38:33,500 --> 00:38:34,715
What's this?
(meowing)

802
00:38:34,740 --> 00:38:35,788
Whoa.

803
00:38:37,860 --> 00:38:39,949
(meowing)
Oh.

804
00:38:40,122 --> 00:38:41,122
(meowing)

805
00:38:42,746 --> 00:38:44,768
It makes different noises
depending on where you touch it.

806
00:38:44,768 --> 00:38:46,944
This was the purring.

807
00:38:48,300 --> 00:38:50,140
(howling)

808
00:38:50,460 --> 00:38:51,768
What the hell was that?

809
00:38:51,792 --> 00:38:53,210
(laughing)

810
00:38:53,340 --> 00:38:56,975
Cat crockery,
cat mugs, cat spoons,

811
00:38:57,860 --> 00:39:00,002
cat dolls, cat glasses,

812
00:39:00,780 --> 00:39:04,100
cat plates, cat posters,
cat stationary,

813
00:39:04,113 --> 00:39:06,588
cat fans, cat everything.

814
00:39:07,952 --> 00:39:11,780
This specialty cat store sells
nothing but cat themed products

815
00:39:12,580 --> 00:39:15,835
and here you can find
practically every household item

816
00:39:15,860 --> 00:39:17,740
to satisfy your cat's obsession.

817
00:39:19,856 --> 00:39:21,285
Cat calendar.

818
00:39:21,300 --> 00:39:22,915
Cat chopsticks.

819
00:39:22,940 --> 00:39:23,988
Cat pocket watch.

820
00:39:24,340 --> 00:39:25,350
Cat umbrellas.

821
00:39:25,555 --> 00:39:26,595
Cat bag.

822
00:39:26,620 --> 00:39:28,590
And of course, cat socks.

823
00:39:29,820 --> 00:39:32,155
So, what do you think
is your most strange

824
00:39:32,180 --> 00:39:34,300
or unique item that you sell?

825
00:39:34,700 --> 00:39:38,217
This is an incense
made from silver vine.

826
00:39:38,253 --> 00:39:41,060
When your cat smells it,

827
00:39:42,060 --> 00:39:44,170
it will be as if it's drunk.

828
00:39:44,220 --> 00:39:46,220
Wow, so it's like
the cat is drunk

829
00:39:46,224 --> 00:39:48,728
when it smells
this stuff (laughs).

830
00:39:49,060 --> 00:39:51,470
Wow, is it popular
with customers?

831
00:39:51,660 --> 00:39:55,478
Recently it's started
to become quite popular.

832
00:39:56,900 --> 00:39:58,475
This store is the one stop shop

833
00:39:58,500 --> 00:40:00,133
for all things cat related,

834
00:40:00,420 --> 00:40:03,035
but what motivated the
owner to open a store

835
00:40:03,060 --> 00:40:05,922
with such a variety of unique
and niche cat products?

836
00:40:07,324 --> 00:40:09,491
I have a few friends who collect

837
00:40:09,516 --> 00:40:12,515
this sort of cat merchandise.

838
00:40:12,557 --> 00:40:15,125
They have to go
to several different stores

839
00:40:15,150 --> 00:40:17,987
and it takes them a lot of time.

840
00:40:18,012 --> 00:40:21,514
So I thought if I gather
everything into one store

841
00:40:21,539 --> 00:40:24,882
they can come here
and get a whole range of things.

842
00:40:25,272 --> 00:40:28,012
So I think this store
makes it a lot easier

843
00:40:28,037 --> 00:40:30,835
for the cat lover.

844
00:40:30,860 --> 00:40:33,405
So I started this store.

845
00:40:34,140 --> 00:40:37,275
I've come across some pretty
odd and quirky products

846
00:40:37,300 --> 00:40:39,995
in this store, however,
I've just gotten my hands

847
00:40:40,020 --> 00:40:42,635
on a rather unusual product
that takes ridiculous

848
00:40:42,660 --> 00:40:43,914
to a whole new level.

849
00:40:46,740 --> 00:40:49,128
This is cat wine,

850
00:40:49,340 --> 00:40:50,707
Nyan Nyan Nouveau.

851
00:40:51,282 --> 00:40:52,595
I'm not making this up either.

852
00:40:52,620 --> 00:40:53,795
This is actually cat wine

853
00:40:53,820 --> 00:40:57,675
because a lot of people in
Japan come home after a long day

854
00:40:57,700 --> 00:40:59,180
sit there
and drink their wine alone,

855
00:40:59,194 --> 00:41:01,116
but what if you could drink
with your cat as well.

856
00:41:01,655 --> 00:41:04,342
That is the premise behind
Nyan Nyan Nouveau wine.

857
00:41:05,710 --> 00:41:07,500
Look, there you go,
there's two cats there.

858
00:41:07,500 --> 00:41:08,952
Is that a cat and a dog?

859
00:41:10,272 --> 00:41:11,952
I don't know if it's just
cats who can drink this,

860
00:41:11,977 --> 00:41:12,995
maybe dogs can as well,

861
00:41:13,020 --> 00:41:16,755
but... I don't know
if humans can drink it,

862
00:41:16,780 --> 00:41:18,660
I don't even know
what it really looks like,

863
00:41:18,860 --> 00:41:19,891
let's find out.

864
00:41:19,916 --> 00:41:22,180
So... pour that in there.

865
00:41:22,233 --> 00:41:23,287
Oh...

866
00:41:25,380 --> 00:41:28,780
The word appetizing
doesn't spring to mind.

867
00:41:30,413 --> 00:41:31,585
Should we try some?

868
00:41:31,585 --> 00:41:33,866
If the cat can drink it,
I can drink it, why not.

869
00:41:36,860 --> 00:41:38,561
(spitting)

870
00:41:39,679 --> 00:41:40,679
(spitting)

871
00:41:42,300 --> 00:41:43,525
Yeah, don't drink cat wine.

872
00:41:43,540 --> 00:41:45,017
Oh man...

873
00:41:47,551 --> 00:41:49,807
(upbeat instrumental music)

874
00:41:49,940 --> 00:41:53,155
Cats are undoubtedly a huge
part of Japanese pop culture,

875
00:41:53,180 --> 00:41:57,060
as seen with characters such
as Doraemon and Hello Kitty.

876
00:41:57,355 --> 00:41:58,435
I've been told there's an entire

877
00:41:58,460 --> 00:42:00,515
Hello Kitty themed hotel room

878
00:42:00,540 --> 00:42:02,714
at an upmarket hotel in Tokyo.

879
00:42:03,100 --> 00:42:04,715
And we're off
to see how much detail

880
00:42:04,740 --> 00:42:08,428
has gone into celebrating the
world famous brand first hand.

881
00:42:10,780 --> 00:42:13,310
Just waiting to go into
the Hello Kitty room.

882
00:42:14,900 --> 00:42:16,286
It's a bit of a giveaway,
isn't it?

883
00:42:16,982 --> 00:42:18,589
Just to make sure you
know which room it is.

884
00:42:19,583 --> 00:42:21,516
Oh, oh my God.

885
00:42:22,362 --> 00:42:23,410
Oh...

886
00:42:24,580 --> 00:42:26,673
Oh, it's like being
in a nightmare.

887
00:42:26,743 --> 00:42:29,962
(playful instrumental music)

888
00:42:31,180 --> 00:42:33,355
With themed trash cans, scales,

889
00:42:33,380 --> 00:42:35,119
toiletries, and water bottles,

890
00:42:35,517 --> 00:42:39,002
there's truly no escaping
Hello Kitty inside the room.

891
00:42:39,980 --> 00:42:42,540
For some, being here
must feel like a dream.

892
00:42:42,728 --> 00:42:44,969
For me,
it's quite disconcerting.

893
00:42:45,980 --> 00:42:49,533
I think one of the reasons
it feels so intense is because

894
00:42:49,940 --> 00:42:52,195
it's not just the walls
that are covered in artwork,

895
00:42:52,220 --> 00:42:54,435
the floor as well
is really colorful,

896
00:42:54,460 --> 00:42:55,820
and there's some artwork there,

897
00:42:55,829 --> 00:42:57,065
and it can be difficult
to work out

898
00:42:57,065 --> 00:42:59,403
where the wall ends and
where the floor begins.

899
00:42:59,900 --> 00:43:02,293
So, it's all just one
big piece of artwork.

900
00:43:03,676 --> 00:43:06,066
You can see the Keio Plaza
on the wall of the hotel,

901
00:43:06,066 --> 00:43:09,108
and this is like a Tokyo
setting, and- oh wow!

902
00:43:09,915 --> 00:43:12,161
- Here you go,
this is a Hello Kitty cake.

903
00:43:12,300 --> 00:43:15,435
- Hello Kitty (laughs),
oh my lord,

904
00:43:15,460 --> 00:43:16,700
a Hello Kitty cake.

905
00:43:17,798 --> 00:43:21,393
But one Hello Kitty themed
hotel room simply isn't enough.

906
00:43:21,900 --> 00:43:23,915
The hotel has another
for customers

907
00:43:23,940 --> 00:43:26,861
who want to appreciated
their favorite cartoon cat

908
00:43:27,060 --> 00:43:28,675
in an opulent atmosphere,

909
00:43:28,700 --> 00:43:30,635
as opposed to the previous room,

910
00:43:30,660 --> 00:43:33,220
which felt like wandering
into a child's nightmare.

911
00:43:34,653 --> 00:43:37,291
I think I prefer this
one to the other one.

912
00:43:37,500 --> 00:43:38,580
I think I like this room.

913
00:43:39,460 --> 00:43:41,300
This feels more
like a hotel room.

914
00:43:41,351 --> 00:43:42,390
-Yeah, right.

915
00:43:42,415 --> 00:43:44,980
And more like a normal hotel
room that's just pink.

916
00:43:45,806 --> 00:43:46,954
This is quite cool.

917
00:43:47,580 --> 00:43:48,885
That's Princess Kitty there.

918
00:43:49,780 --> 00:43:52,100
I'm particularly
excited about this chair,

919
00:43:52,660 --> 00:43:54,181
this is very cool, isn't it?

920
00:43:55,490 --> 00:43:57,738
So, you also have
Hello Kitty breakfast.

921
00:43:57,980 --> 00:43:59,355
- Kitty on omelets.

922
00:43:59,380 --> 00:44:01,905
- Oh my God,
Hello Kitty on the omelet.

923
00:44:01,930 --> 00:44:04,829
- And a Hello Kitty sandwich.
- A Hello Kitty sandwich.

924
00:44:06,540 --> 00:44:10,140
Yeah, that's a pretty
thoroughly

925
00:44:10,174 --> 00:44:12,550
Hello Kitty branded
breakfast experience.

926
00:44:12,575 --> 00:44:13,593
- (laughs) yeah.

927
00:44:14,212 --> 00:44:17,459
(slow instrumental music)

928
00:44:17,940 --> 00:44:18,976
As I mentioned earlier,

929
00:44:18,994 --> 00:44:21,848
Japan is actually home
to several cat islands.

930
00:44:22,100 --> 00:44:23,522
Some are more
well known than others,

931
00:44:23,522 --> 00:44:26,235
and Enoshima is one that's
gotten some attention

932
00:44:26,260 --> 00:44:27,420
for being a cat island.

933
00:44:27,900 --> 00:44:29,955
However, unlike Tashirojima,
this one

934
00:44:29,980 --> 00:44:31,300
can be accessed on foot.

935
00:44:31,620 --> 00:44:34,980
(mid-tempo instrumental music)

936
00:44:36,300 --> 00:44:38,655
It's a pretty big contrast
to Tashirojima.

937
00:44:39,444 --> 00:44:42,351
The abandoned
Jurassic Park style island.

938
00:44:42,827 --> 00:44:44,601
This is a far cry from that.

939
00:44:44,773 --> 00:44:46,309
This is one of the most
busiest tourist spots

940
00:44:46,309 --> 00:44:47,768
I've ever seen in Japan.

941
00:44:50,291 --> 00:44:52,312
Enoshima is only a short trip
from Tokyo,

942
00:44:52,312 --> 00:44:55,933
which makes it an extremely
popular hot spot for tourists.

943
00:44:56,580 --> 00:44:58,540
With this many people
coming and going though,

944
00:44:58,820 --> 00:45:00,940
it seems like it wouldn't
be idea for cats,

945
00:45:01,265 --> 00:45:04,725
so it's time to console a
giant novelty tourist map.

946
00:45:06,300 --> 00:45:07,640
Cat, cat, cat.

947
00:45:08,481 --> 00:45:10,441
Let's go and see if
there's actually some cats

948
00:45:10,540 --> 00:45:11,780
at that spot on the map.

949
00:45:11,860 --> 00:45:12,989
It's just around the corner.

950
00:45:13,860 --> 00:45:17,645
And up a flight of stairs,
oh my God, up stairs.

951
00:45:19,260 --> 00:45:21,780
The locations on the map lead
me away from the tourists

952
00:45:21,860 --> 00:45:24,296
over to the residential
side of the island,

953
00:45:24,820 --> 00:45:28,235
and sure enough, I've
finally found our first cat

954
00:45:28,260 --> 00:45:31,127
dozing directly underneath
this small shrine.

955
00:45:31,860 --> 00:45:34,777
I've never seen
a cat sit so still.

956
00:45:36,205 --> 00:45:37,339
I don't even know if it's real,

957
00:45:37,339 --> 00:45:38,815
I think it's just a toy.

958
00:45:39,713 --> 00:45:41,655
There's two cats here
relaxing under a tree.

959
00:45:41,900 --> 00:45:43,819
I'm quite curious to see
how many more we can find.

960
00:45:44,655 --> 00:45:47,819
The residential part of
Enoshima is quiet and peaceful,

961
00:45:47,980 --> 00:45:50,202
a stark contrast
to the tourist side.

962
00:45:50,663 --> 00:45:53,275
And as I walk these
gentle tranquil streets,

963
00:45:53,300 --> 00:45:55,517
I'm greeted by more
and more cats.

964
00:45:56,420 --> 00:45:59,674
It turns out Enoshima is
indeed a cat island of sorts.

965
00:45:59,980 --> 00:46:03,300
Though very different to the
dense cat chaos of Tashirojima,

966
00:46:03,620 --> 00:46:05,364
it does have its own quiet charm

967
00:46:05,660 --> 00:46:08,442
with cats spread out
across parts of the island.

968
00:46:08,620 --> 00:46:11,035
(slow instrumental music)

969
00:46:12,239 --> 00:46:14,160
On a scale of one
to stylish cat,

970
00:46:14,660 --> 00:46:16,580
this is a stylish cat,
look at that mustache.

971
00:46:16,700 --> 00:46:17,796
That is glorious.

972
00:46:18,163 --> 00:46:19,636
I think one
main difference between

973
00:46:19,636 --> 00:46:21,622
Enoshima and Tashirojima,

974
00:46:21,900 --> 00:46:23,995
on Tashirojima
there's cats everywhere,

975
00:46:24,020 --> 00:46:25,093
they're not difficult to find.

976
00:46:25,380 --> 00:46:26,915
You turn a street
and there's half a dozen

977
00:46:26,940 --> 00:46:28,069
cats walking around.

978
00:46:28,555 --> 00:46:30,315
Here on Enoshima, you really
have to search for them,

979
00:46:30,340 --> 00:46:32,380
it's like a cat treasure hunt.

980
00:46:33,460 --> 00:46:34,700
Every time you find one,
you feel like

981
00:46:34,739 --> 00:46:35,810
you've achieved something.

982
00:46:36,319 --> 00:46:38,835
And sometimes
you get a little bonus,

983
00:46:38,860 --> 00:46:40,154
and they've got a mustache.

984
00:46:40,624 --> 00:46:41,624
(meowing)

985
00:46:41,950 --> 00:46:45,256
(slow instrumental music)

986
00:46:47,660 --> 00:46:50,115
Whilst Hello Kitty may
have taken the world by storm,

987
00:46:50,140 --> 00:46:52,020
and become
an international icon,

988
00:46:52,340 --> 00:46:54,155
I'm off to meet
the creator of perhaps,

989
00:46:54,180 --> 00:46:56,472
Japan's most iconic
cat character,

990
00:46:56,644 --> 00:46:58,555
which can be found
all across the country

991
00:46:58,580 --> 00:47:01,027
on merchandise,
posters, and billboards.

992
00:47:03,929 --> 00:47:06,475
(speaking Japanese)

993
00:47:06,500 --> 00:47:07,832
- Nice to meet you.

994
00:47:07,900 --> 00:47:09,176
(speaking Japanese)

995
00:47:09,202 --> 00:47:10,434
- And thank you very much
for today.

996
00:47:12,380 --> 00:47:14,315
This is Satoru Tsuda,

997
00:47:14,340 --> 00:47:16,294
the creator of Nameneko.

998
00:47:16,540 --> 00:47:18,660
Though mostly unknown
outside of Japan,

999
00:47:18,900 --> 00:47:22,260
Nameneko was a hugely
popular brand in the 1980s,

1000
00:47:22,380 --> 00:47:24,955
and is often credited
with single-handedly

1001
00:47:24,980 --> 00:47:27,540
starting cat pop culture
across Japan.

1002
00:47:28,060 --> 00:47:29,875
It started when Mr. Tsuda,

1003
00:47:29,900 --> 00:47:31,355
a photographer by trade,

1004
00:47:31,380 --> 00:47:32,926
began photographing cats

1005
00:47:32,951 --> 00:47:34,660
wearing
his partner's doll's clothes.

1006
00:47:35,220 --> 00:47:38,860
The unique photos went on to
sell over eight million copies,

1007
00:47:38,871 --> 00:47:40,402
and a brand was born.

1008
00:47:41,380 --> 00:47:43,566
These are all articles
and magazines,

1009
00:47:44,180 --> 00:47:47,395
newspapers where
the cats have appeared.

1010
00:47:47,420 --> 00:47:49,900
(laughs) Smoking.

1011
00:47:51,180 --> 00:47:53,998
This is a real picture,
not synthesized.

1012
00:47:54,468 --> 00:47:56,547
(laughing)

1013
00:47:56,820 --> 00:47:58,100
I think that's
the best thing about it.

1014
00:47:58,140 --> 00:48:00,835
It's not... digital
photo manipulation.

1015
00:48:00,860 --> 00:48:03,528
Those are actually cats
dressed up.

1016
00:48:04,220 --> 00:48:07,294
Ah, there's an advert
for Microsoft.

1017
00:48:09,060 --> 00:48:11,486
So, this is a Japanese
rice cracker...

1018
00:48:11,511 --> 00:48:12,832
style product, Senbei.

1019
00:48:13,334 --> 00:48:15,466
A lot of people thought
it was for cats

1020
00:48:15,914 --> 00:48:17,343
because it looks like pet food,

1021
00:48:17,343 --> 00:48:18,688
what with the cat there.

1022
00:48:19,085 --> 00:48:20,253
So, on the second edition,

1023
00:48:20,253 --> 00:48:23,188
they had to put here,
"It's for humans," so...

1024
00:48:23,300 --> 00:48:24,980
(chuckles) just so people
would know.

1025
00:48:27,060 --> 00:48:31,021
So, these are specially
designed cat clothes.

1026
00:48:31,076 --> 00:48:32,076
(laughs)

1027
00:48:32,220 --> 00:48:35,200
They cost, I think,
about $1,500 each,

1028
00:48:35,622 --> 00:48:38,395
and they're hand made
to perfection.

1029
00:48:38,420 --> 00:48:40,820
They're so detailed
and intricate.

1030
00:48:41,060 --> 00:48:42,766
They look better
than human clothes.

1031
00:48:43,180 --> 00:48:47,055
That is more expensive
than an Armani suit

1032
00:48:47,180 --> 00:48:50,328
because it's tailor made,
uh... for a cat.

1033
00:48:50,940 --> 00:48:52,208
(laughs)

1034
00:48:52,232 --> 00:48:53,867
It's rather impressive
and surreal.

1035
00:48:57,396 --> 00:48:59,395
These images were taken
long before

1036
00:48:59,420 --> 00:49:01,100
the arrival of Photoshop.

1037
00:49:01,340 --> 00:49:03,355
All of the pictures
are of real cats

1038
00:49:03,380 --> 00:49:05,700
with custom made props
and costumes.

1039
00:49:05,954 --> 00:49:08,595
But how did a few cats
in upmarket clothes

1040
00:49:08,620 --> 00:49:10,980
go on to become
a national sensation?

1041
00:49:13,340 --> 00:49:15,968
So, what is the history
of Nameneko?

1042
00:49:16,340 --> 00:49:20,700
The Nameneko brand
started in 1980.

1043
00:49:21,420 --> 00:49:25,634
It all started when I found
four abandoned kittens.

1044
00:49:26,314 --> 00:49:30,769
I opened a discarded
cardboard box and found

1045
00:49:30,794 --> 00:49:33,628
the newborns which were so small

1046
00:49:33,660 --> 00:49:37,401
that I couldn't even tell
that they were kittens.

1047
00:49:37,420 --> 00:49:41,091
I cleaned and dried them off,

1048
00:49:41,116 --> 00:49:44,179
and I realized
they were kittens when I saw

1049
00:49:44,204 --> 00:49:48,409
their fur fluff up
for the first time.

1050
00:49:49,340 --> 00:49:54,180
My partner was designing clothes
for French dolls,

1051
00:49:54,820 --> 00:49:59,028
and one day she left them
at my house.

1052
00:49:59,620 --> 00:50:03,740
The cats were playing with them
and had damaged them.

1053
00:50:03,781 --> 00:50:07,366
The clothes could
no longer be sold,

1054
00:50:07,391 --> 00:50:10,779
so I dressed the cats up
in the clothes.

1055
00:50:10,804 --> 00:50:14,893
I snapped a few photos,
and when I showed my friends

1056
00:50:14,918 --> 00:50:18,050
they all thought
the cats looked adorable.

1057
00:50:18,075 --> 00:50:21,444
They suggested
I publish these photos,

1058
00:50:21,469 --> 00:50:23,962
and that was the start
of Nameneko.

1059
00:50:24,940 --> 00:50:28,822
(soft instrumental music)

1060
00:50:29,370 --> 00:50:32,059
With my journey across the
country coming to an end,

1061
00:50:32,260 --> 00:50:34,755
I must say I'm as bewildered
as ever

1062
00:50:34,780 --> 00:50:37,057
by Japan's fascination
with cats.

1063
00:50:37,860 --> 00:50:39,780
Cats with jobs,
cat themed stores,

1064
00:50:39,780 --> 00:50:42,900
and cats in, well, odd places.

1065
00:50:43,041 --> 00:50:47,555
Japan's cat antics are both
intriguing and entertaining,

1066
00:50:47,580 --> 00:50:50,260
and though some may find
it just plain weird,

1067
00:50:50,285 --> 00:50:51,788
one thing is for sure,

1068
00:50:52,100 --> 00:50:55,300
Japan is the cat capital
of the world.

1069
00:50:55,603 --> 00:50:59,055
(music flourishes, fades out)

1070
00:51:03,375 --> 00:51:07,125
(bright instrumental music)

